# Files Fern must not modify or delete when regenerating this repo.
#
# Fern owns the SDK source and its ci.yml, and prunes anything it did not generate — it
# reads this file from the pull request's base branch, so an entry only protects a file
# once it is on main.
#
# publish-main.yml is hand-written: it releases whop-sdk when a merge to main lands a
# [tool.poetry] version that is not yet on PyPI. It is the only publish path — the
# Stainless machinery (release-please, publish-pypi.yml, release-doctor.yml, bin/) was
# removed with the cutover.
#
# src/whop_sdk/lib holds verify_user_token, the one hand-written helper in this SDK. It
# depends only on the standard library and pyjwt, so it survives the generated client
# being replaced. The [user-tokens] extra that declares pyjwt does not survive — see the
# cutover notes in the monorepo's sdks/fern/README.md.
.github/workflows/publish-main.yml
src/whop_sdk/lib
